  "description": "DAU on the daily, streak length, and freeze usage (SPEC §14).\n\n**`daily.streak_broken` does not exist and is not coming.** Nothing on the client is told when a streak ends — the streak is folded from stored results on every read, so a broken one is simply a smaller number next time somebody asks. Firing the event would need a remembered 'streak as of last read' to compare against, which is exactly the counter the design refuses. The streak histogram on this board is the same fact from the other side.\n\n**Daily events carry no `level_id`.** A daily board is a position in the daily pool and the two packs share a number line, so a `level_id` here would silently mix with campaign ids. Anything per-board about the daily has to come from `game.level_started`/`game.level_completed` with `mode=\"daily\"` instead.\n\n**Loki-backed, so nothing here can see past Grafana Cloud's log retention.** Widening the time picker does not widen the answer.\n\n**Delivery is at-least-once.** A record can rarely ship twice (export acknowledged, process died before the buffer delete), so read raw counts as approximate. Panels that count *installs* rather than records are immune to it by construction — a duplicate lands in the same `install_id` series and collapses.",
  "editable": true,
  "fiscalYearStartMonth": 0,
  "graphTooltip": 0,
  "links": [],
