    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "loki",
        "uid": "grafanacloud-logs"
      },
      "description": "One observation per install: the longest streak it reached.\n\nThe shape that matters is the tail. A wall at 1 and 2 with nothing beyond means the daily is a thing people try rather than a habit they keep, and the fix is the reason to come back on day 3, not the board on day 1.\n\n**There is no `daily.streak_broken` event** — nothing on the client is told when a streak ends, because the streak is folded from stored results on every read. A break is simply a smaller number next time somebody asks, which is what this histogram is made of.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "fillOpacity": 80,
